{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): \"log\" without a base\nambiguous: set args.assume.log to one of:\n  1) the natural log, ln (default)\n  2) log base 2\n  3) log base 10\nrepeat the request with args.assume.log set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"natural log\", \"log base 2\" or \"log base 10\", or \"assume log means base 2\""}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": false, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is the log of x for x from 1 to 8?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": [], "understood": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "\"log\" without a base", "key": "log", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "the natural log, ln", "default": true}, {"index": 2, "reading": "log base 2", "default": false}, {"index": 3, "reading": "log base 10", "default": false}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.log set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"natural log\", \"log base 2\" or \"log base 10\", or \"assume log means base 2\""}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: \"log\" without a base: log base 2 (kept for this session)\n  ucas: it(x in 1..8) = log(x)/log(2)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: int in 1..8) = log(real(x))/0.6931471806\n  -> real\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "\u001eanswer 2\nwhat is the log of x for x from 1 to 8?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x in 1..8) = log(x)/log(2)", "show it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "show", "definition": "it(x: int in 1..8) = log(real(x))/0.6931471806", "body": "log(real(x))/0.6931471806", "type": "real"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "\"log\" without a base: log base 2 (kept for this session)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: \"log\" without a base: log base 2 (kept for this session)\n  ucas: it(x in 1..8) = log(x)/log(2)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: int in 1..8) = log(real(x))/0.6931471806\n  -> real\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x in 1..8) = log(x)/log(2)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: int in 1..8) = log(real(x))/0.6931471806\n  -> real\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "\u001eanswer 1\nwhat is the log of x for x from 1 to 8?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x in 1..8) = log(x)/log(2)", "show it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "show", "definition": "it(x: int in 1..8) = log(real(x))/0.6931471806", "body": "log(real(x))/0.6931471806", "type": "real"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x in 1..8) = log(x)/log(2)\n  ucas: show it\nit(x: int in 1..8) = log(real(x))/0.6931471806\n  -> real\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): \"even\"\nambiguous: set args.assume.question to one of:\n  1) an even function, f(-x) = f(x) (default)\n  2) an even number for every input\nrepeat the request with args.assume.question set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"an even function\" or \"always even\""}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": false, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x*x even for x: u8", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": [], "understood": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "\"even\"", "key": "question", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "an even function, f(-x) = f(x)", "default": true}, {"index": 2, "reading": "an even number for every input", "default": false}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.question set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"an even function\" or \"always even\""}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x*x\n  ucas: parity it\nparity of it:\n  even: f(-x) = f(x)\n  proved, exhaustive, with -x and -f(x) in u8 arithmetic (two's complement: -x is 2^w - x)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "\u001eanswer 1\nis x*x even for x: u8", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: u8) = x*x", "parity it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "parity", "even": "f(-x) = f(x)", "headline": "parity of it:", "details": ["proved, exhaustive, with -x and -f(x) in u8 arithmetic (two's complement: -x is 2^w - x)"]}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: u8) = x*x\n  ucas: parity it\nparity of it:\n  even: f(-x) = f(x)\n  proved, exhaustive, with -x and -f(x) in u8 arithmetic (two's complement: -x is 2^w - x)\n"}, "isError": false}}
