{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: no interval given: using -pi/2 to pi/2 (say \"on a to b\")\n  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)\n  ucas: approx it in -pi/2..pi/2 method cheb\n  note: \"0 to pi/4 degree 4 nocrit\" is not one of the 2 choices for it has special points at the interval's ends (at x = -1.57079633 a minimum, at x = 1.57079633 a maximum): bounds a caller may rely on; keep them exact (costs some error elsewhere): read as no, fit freely\napprox it on [-1.57079637, 1.57079637] as f32, fma\n  checked: it is odd (f(-x) = -f(x) at 64 points): fitting x*P(x^2) on [0, 1.57079637]\n  metric: relative error\n  checked: the target equals sin(x) at 33 points: range reductions and identities for sin apply\n  fits in real arithmetic (max relative error of x*P(x^2)):\n    deg  cheb interp  cheb econ    minimax\n    1    0.267        0.276        0.222        \n    3    0.00885      0.00898      0.00721      \n    5    0.000134     0.000135     0.000108     \n    7    1.17e-06     1.18e-06     9.39e-07     \n    9    6.65e-09     6.68e-09     5.31e-09     \n    11   2.65e-11     2.66e-11     2.12e-11     \n  Chebyshev interpolation polynomial of it, degree 9 (max relative error 6.65e-09 in real arithmetic, the lowest degree that reaches the format's precision):\n    it(x) = 2.605107627e-06*x^9 - 0.0001980901741*x^7 + 0.008333050171*x^5 - 0.1666665795*x^3 + 0.9999999957*x\n    in the Chebyshev basis: 1.133648188*T1(u) - 0.1380717869*T3(u) + 0.004490714845*T5(u) - 6.770130203e-05*T7(u) + 5.92467739e-07*T9(u)\n      where u = x/1.570796371 maps [-1.57079637, 1.57079637] to [-1, 1]\n    other degrees: add `degree n`; the other methods and shapes: add `compare`\n  candidates ranked by max ulp and cost under gt1030 (sampled floats); defined as ap1..:\n  measured on 131102 f32 in [-1.57079637, 1.57079637]; ulp against the exact value (naive rounding in parentheses)\n  #   kind      deg   form        error (naive)            max rel       max abs       cost\n  1   cheb      3     horner+fma  1.48e+05 ulp             0.00885       0.00885       3    at x=1.57079637\n      x*P(x^2): x*fma(-0.147131488, s, 0.994019866) where s = x*x\n      rounding of ap1, first order, 3 operations, relative, in u = 2^-24: worst case 2.58, probable no better (under 16 operations), expected 0.881; `error ap1 ~ F` says what each means\n  2   cheb      5     horner+fma  2.25e+03 ulp             0.000134      0.000134      4    at x=-1.57079637\n      x*P(x^2): x*fma(fma(0.00762666203, s, -0.166020006), s, 0.999911547) where s = x*x\n  3   cheb      7     horner+fma  19.6 ulp (21)            1.18e-06      1.17e-06      5    at x=-1.46006048\n      x*P(x^2): fma(x*s, fma(fma(-0.000185423036, s, 0.00831427798), s, -0.166658536), x) where s = x*x\n  4   cheb      9     horner+fma  1.53 ulp (1.53)          9.1e-08       9.09e-08      6    at x=-1.5408833\n      x*P(x^2): fma(x*s, fma(fma(fma(2.60609568e-06, s, -0.000198097769), s, 0.00833306927), s, -0.166666597), x) where s = x*x\n  5 more: 'approx more [n]' (dominated or worse)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "\u001eanswer 0 to pi/4 degree 4 nocrit\napprox sin using cheby poly", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = sin(x)", "approx it in -pi/2..pi/2 method cheb"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "approx", "function": "it", "lo": -1.5707963705062866, "hi": 1.5707963705062866, "metric": "max ulp", "model": "gt1030", "format": "f32", "sample_points": 131102, "exhaustive": false, "candidates": [{"rank": 1, "name": "ap1", "kind": "cheb", "degree": "3", "form": "horner+fma", "shape": "x*P(x^2)", "expr": "x*fma(-0.147131488, s, 0.994019866) where s = x*x", "max_rel_error": 0.008847177028655059, "max_abs_error": 0.00884717702865505, "max_ulp": 148430.99999998396, "worst_at": 1.5707963705062866, "cost": 3, "meets_target": false}, {"rank": 2, "name": "ap2", "kind": "cheb", "degree": "5", "form": "horner+fma", "shape": "x*P(x^2)", "expr": "x*fma(fma(0.00762666203, s, -0.166020006), s, 0.999911547) where s = x*x", "max_rel_error": 0.00013422966003513517, "max_abs_error": 0.00013422966003513503, "max_ulp": 2252.000000016028, "worst_at": -1.5707963705062866, "cost": 4, "meets_target": false}, {"rank": 3, "name": "ap3", "kind": "cheb", "degree": "7", "form": "horner+fma", "shape": "x*P(x^2)", "expr": "fma(x*s, fma(fma(-0.000185423036, s, 0.00831427798), s, -0.166658536), x) where s = x*x", "max_rel_error": 1.1774565702714118e-06, "max_abs_error": 1.1702447059452762e-06, "max_ulp": 19.633448204500382, "naive_ulp": 20.999999983971975, "worst_at": -1.460060477256775, "cost": 5, "meets_target": false}, {"rank": 4, "name": "ap4", "kind": "cheb", "degree": "9", "form": "horner+fma", "shape": "x*P(x^2)", "expr": "fma(x*s, fma(fma(fma(2.60609568e-06, s, -0.000198097769), s, 0.00833306927), s, -0.166666597), x) where s = x*x", "max_rel_error": 9.096274234553025e-08, "max_abs_error": 9.092204914884581e-08, "max_ulp": 1.5254188577328023, "naive_ulp": 1.5317186678948929, "worst_at": -1.5408833026885986, "cost": 6, "meets_target": false}], "more": 5}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "no interval given: using -pi/2 to pi/2 (say \"on a to b\")"}, {"kind": "rule", "text": "\"0 to pi/4 degree 4 nocrit\" is not one of the 2 choices for it has special points at the interval's ends (at x = -1.57079633 a minimum, at x = 1.57079633 a maximum): bounds a caller may rely on; keep them exact (costs some error elsewhere): read as no, fit freely"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: no interval given: using -pi/2 to pi/2 (say \"on a to b\")\n  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)\n  ucas: approx it in -pi/2..pi/2 method cheb\n  note: \"0 to pi/4 degree 4 nocrit\" is not one of the 2 choices for it has special points at the interval's ends (at x = -1.57079633 a minimum, at x = 1.57079633 a maximum): bounds a caller may rely on; keep them exact (costs some error elsewhere): r